WEBVTT

00:00:07.210 --> 00:00:08.740
They've arrived.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.590
At last?

00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:14.790
What a troublesome brother I have.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:19.290
Why must he always make me worry so?

00:00:19.290 --> 00:00:23.640
Of course, given his strength, there's no need to worry,

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:26.270
but you never know what could happen!

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:31.590
And not only that, what if he were to attract the attention of some weird girl?

00:00:31.590 --> 00:00:35.280
Ugh! I just can't help but worry!

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:42.040
Big Brother...

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.630
To our safe return to the capital, 
and in welcome of new friends made!{merged}

00:02:17.880 --> 00:02:19.380
Cheers!

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.730
Drink up, drink up!

00:02:22.190 --> 00:02:23.890
"Drink up, drink up,"

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:25.760
is <i>not</i> what I want to hear.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.920
Huh? Who's that?

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:31.020
Yay!

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.020
We've been waiting for you!

00:02:33.020 --> 00:02:35.960
Nekone-chan!

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.780
Nekone?

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:43.850
What do you think you're doing?

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:45.910
Uh, what do you...

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:49.040
I'll ask again. What do you think you're doing?

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:50.750
Oh, Nekone.

00:02:50.750 --> 00:02:52.710
Good timing.

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.460
Come on, join me.

00:02:54.460 --> 00:02:56.670
No, Big Brother, I will <i>not</i> join you!

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.400
"Big Brother"?

00:02:58.400 --> 00:03:00.380
You have a little sister, Ukon?

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:01.360
Her?

00:03:02.590 --> 00:03:04.010
What, surprised?

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.560
You mean... she's not your daughter?

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:08.430
"Daughter"!?

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.310
Always got something funny to say, don't you, kid?

00:03:16.940 --> 00:03:20.940
A-Anyway, you finally return home,

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:23.270
and the first thing you do is go drinking?

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:25.820
Do you know how worried I've been?

00:03:25.820 --> 00:03:28.070
Don't be like that.

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:29.830
It's all part of the job.

00:03:30.260 --> 00:03:31.080
Hey,{split}

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:33.580
that's the ribbon I gave you!{split}

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:36.330
It looks good on you.

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:42.280
St-Stop trying to change the subject, Big Brother!

00:03:45.660 --> 00:03:46.840
Sorry,

00:03:46.840 --> 00:03:48.760
but there's something I need you to do.

00:03:50.170 --> 00:03:51.520
You see...

00:03:54.090 --> 00:03:57.900
Well, I think it's time to try out Hakuroukaku's famous baths!

00:03:58.140 --> 00:04:00.660
Oh, a drink in a hot bath, huh?

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:01.350
Sounds great!

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:02.900
Big Brother, honestly!

00:04:02.900 --> 00:04:04.150
A bath!

00:04:04.910 --> 00:04:06.980
Hot water...

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.530
Soft, smooth skin...

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:11.500
Oh, no! The seal's been broken!

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:12.880
Run, Rurutie!

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.580
Hot water!

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:20.250
A bath!

00:04:26.890 --> 00:04:28.600
It's a bath! A hot bath!

00:04:33.310 --> 00:04:35.590
Come on, everyone, hop in!

00:04:35.590 --> 00:04:39.080
It's a bath! Get in! It's so great!

00:04:40.810 --> 00:04:45.960
U-Um... I've never been in a place like this before.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.430
Um...

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:49.410
Uh, Kuon-san...

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.600
Do baths really get you that excited?

00:04:55.710 --> 00:04:58.920
You know, I think we can do without these!

00:05:00.920 --> 00:05:03.140
Wh-What are you doing?

00:05:03.140 --> 00:05:04.860
This is the best!

00:05:04.860 --> 00:05:08.180
I've always wanted to take a bath with my friends!

00:05:08.530 --> 00:05:10.260
F-Friends?

00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:13.210
I don't really care about that...

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:15.060
Don't be silly.

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.890
Any little sister of Ukon is a little sister of mine too!

00:05:18.890 --> 00:05:20.810
You can let me spoil you!

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:22.820
W-Wait a second!

00:05:23.110 --> 00:05:26.260
What exactly is your 
relationship with my brother?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.200
What's that smile supposed to mean?

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:33.550
Sounds like they're having the time of their lives over there.

00:05:33.550 --> 00:05:36.960
Kuon becomes a totally different person when baths are involved.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:41.250
So what're your future plans, kid?

00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:44.960
You can't hang around the young miss and have her feed you the rest of your life.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.190
It'll work out somehow.

00:05:50.760 --> 00:05:53.880
I do like how easygoing you are, but...

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.310
Me, too!

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:05.110
They're sure kicking up a racket over there.

00:06:05.110 --> 00:06:08.360
Baths are supposed to be quiet and refined.

00:06:08.360 --> 00:06:11.990
Be straight with me. Is there really nothing going on between you and my brother?

00:06:12.640 --> 00:06:14.260
Relax, I was just teasing.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:18.250
I think Ukon's closer to Haku than me, anyway.

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:21.610
They're probably enjoying the bath together right now.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.510
Haku-san?

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:29.760
H-Haku-sama and Ukon-sama are bathing together?

00:06:30.880 --> 00:06:33.260
And they're both naked...

00:06:37.240 --> 00:06:38.890
Rurutie-sama!

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:41.030
Hey, uh,

00:06:41.030 --> 00:06:43.150
is that really your little sister?{split}

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.130
You know it.

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:48.340
The way her tail bends is just like mine, right?

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:54.030
Master Nekone is the youngest person ever to pass the most difficult exam in this country.

00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.280
Such is her talent.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:57.990
That's quite a feat.

00:06:58.950 --> 00:07:04.540
Of course, she's so young that they still won't accept her as a scholar.

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:09.220
Anyway, I've got a question for you, too.

00:07:09.220 --> 00:07:12.550
Are you and Miss Kuon an item?

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.640
Huh? Of course not.{merge}

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:18.060
What, is this some sort of one-sided thing then?

00:07:18.560 --> 00:07:20.880
It's not like that.

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:22.870
It's more like...

00:07:23.790 --> 00:07:25.930
I'm Haku's...

00:07:25.930 --> 00:07:28.110
guardian, you could say?

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:31.340
Nothing more, nothing less.

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:32.550
I see.

00:07:32.550 --> 00:07:35.120
So you're like a mother and child?

00:07:36.800 --> 00:07:39.280
Do I look that old to you?

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:41.370
I-I'm sorry!

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:45.750
But who <i>is</i> that Haku guy?

00:07:46.300 --> 00:07:49.720
He certainly didn't look very strong.

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:50.760
Are you curious?

00:07:52.480 --> 00:07:55.510
My brother seemed to enjoy his company.

00:07:56.130 --> 00:07:57.650
You know how he is.

00:07:57.650 --> 00:08:00.840
But still, there are only a few people he really trusts.

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.320
That's true.

00:08:03.320 --> 00:08:06.060
Haku has this strange charisma.

00:08:06.650 --> 00:08:08.870
If you're curious, try talking to him tomorrow.

00:08:09.490 --> 00:08:11.820
Haku-sama's strange charisma...

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.320
makes Ukon-sama happy?

00:08:24.710 --> 00:08:26.500
Good morning to you all.

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:32.040
Do we <i>have</i> to leave this early?

00:08:32.040 --> 00:08:35.760
Nekone has graciously offered to show us around the capital.

00:08:36.170 --> 00:08:37.060
Okay?

00:08:37.060 --> 00:08:39.220
That's how it worked out.

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:40.970
Well then, let's go.

00:08:40.970 --> 00:08:42.020
We're leaving.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:47.520
<i>Today I'll get a good look at the true nature of this Haku-san my brother has opened up to.</i>

00:08:48.890 --> 00:08:51.420
This is the main street.

00:08:51.420 --> 00:08:54.150
This sure is a big city.

00:08:55.110 --> 00:08:57.300
How far does this street go?

00:08:57.300 --> 00:09:00.910
It goes north, all the way to the palace.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:04.950
This must've been a pain to build.

00:09:04.950 --> 00:09:07.920
This city was built by the Emperor himself.

00:09:08.430 --> 00:09:11.450
I heard that was centuries ago, though.

00:09:11.450 --> 00:09:12.500
I see.

00:09:12.500 --> 00:09:15.300
So it's the work of the Emperor who was alive then.

00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.530
Huh?

00:09:16.530 --> 00:09:20.300
The Emperor is still there in the palace.

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:22.650
For centuries?

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:25.430
Wait, am I the only one who thinks that's strange?

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:28.940
Oddly enough, it seems to be true.

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:32.190
The Emperor is omniscient and omnipotent.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.570
It's arrogant to even try to measure him by your own standards.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:37.910
I see.

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.670
Well, if that's what people claim, then that's that.

00:09:40.670 --> 00:09:43.330
It's not just what people claim! It's true!

00:09:43.880 --> 00:09:46.870
<i>This is why I hate country bumpkins.</i>

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:53.380
Is this the Divine Court I've heard so much about?

00:09:53.380 --> 00:09:54.550
It's so pretty!

00:09:54.550 --> 00:09:55.840
That's right.

00:09:56.400 --> 00:09:58.970
Hey, what's it made of?

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:01.080
This is a holy place.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:03.470
It's made of holy things.

00:10:04.700 --> 00:10:06.150
Holy, you say?

00:10:06.150 --> 00:10:09.700
Things the uneducated such as yourself wouldn't know about.{Mugaku - uneducated}

00:10:09.700 --> 00:10:10.790
If you say so.

00:10:10.790 --> 00:10:13.230
I don't know much about that stuff.

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:17.480
<i>What's with this guy?</i>

00:10:17.480 --> 00:10:20.210
<i>He's like a dimwitted child!</i>

00:10:24.740 --> 00:10:26.360
Welcome!

00:10:26.650 --> 00:10:28.250
It's pretty noisy here.

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.000
I think the word you're looking for is "lively."

00:10:31.470 --> 00:10:32.820
Lively?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:34.310
Really?

00:10:34.310 --> 00:10:36.090
<i>He always talks back.</i>

00:10:36.090 --> 00:10:37.890
<i>What an irritating man.</i>

00:10:37.890 --> 00:10:39.180
Oshutaru-sama!

00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:41.070
Oshutaru-sama!

00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:43.760
Oshutaru-sama!

00:10:44.650 --> 00:10:46.150
Oshutaru-sama!

00:10:46.530 --> 00:10:48.170
He must be performing an inspection.

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.900
He's really popular!

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:51.140
I don't get it.

00:10:51.140 --> 00:10:53.270
Is he that amazing?

00:10:53.270 --> 00:10:55.150
Wh-What are you saying!?

00:10:55.530 --> 00:10:58.650
He's a hundred, no, a thousand times more amazing than you!

00:10:59.100 --> 00:11:01.600
It's arrogant to even compare yourself to him!

00:11:01.600 --> 00:11:03.440
You should apologize!

00:11:03.440 --> 00:11:04.780
Oh, right...

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:05.910
Sorry.

00:11:11.630 --> 00:11:13.940
We should get going, Kuon-san.

00:11:14.830 --> 00:11:17.920
Okay, we've gotten a pretty good feel for the capital.

00:11:18.680 --> 00:11:21.030
It's time to move on to today's main event.{, I think.}

00:11:21.030 --> 00:11:23.320
We're going somewhere <i>else</i>?

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:25.520
My legs are killing me.

00:11:25.520 --> 00:11:29.060
Haku-san, what are you going to do after this?

00:11:29.230 --> 00:11:33.060
Well, I'm going to go back to the inn, have a drink...

00:11:33.060 --> 00:11:34.810
That's not what I meant.

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.570
I'm asking how you plan to get by from tomorrow onward.

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:43.300
Kuon-san tells me she's been looking after you because you're jobless.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.240
Ukon asked me the same thing.

00:11:45.960 --> 00:11:49.370
Well, I'll cross that bridge when I get to it.

00:11:50.970 --> 00:11:54.040
That's the typical thought process of a failure.

00:11:54.040 --> 00:11:58.230
Haku-sama isn't a failure...

00:11:58.230 --> 00:12:00.980
Yeah, you tell 'er!

00:12:00.980 --> 00:12:03.880
Let's put those words to the test, then, shall we?

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:08.010
Let's find you a job!

00:12:08.680 --> 00:12:09.510
Huh?{added}{we've done all the other Huhs so it'd be weird to skip this one}

00:12:10.810 --> 00:12:12.020
What!?{added}

00:12:16.780 --> 00:12:20.150
Is it really a good idea to make him deal with customers so soon?

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:24.260
We can always try something else if it doesn't work out.

00:12:24.260 --> 00:12:27.160
G-Good luck, Haku-sama!

00:12:29.080 --> 00:12:30.800
Here's your food.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.840
This isn't what I ordered.

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:34.960
Oh, really?

00:12:34.960 --> 00:12:37.360
Sorry man, I'll switch this.

00:12:37.360 --> 00:12:40.540
Whoa, hold on. That's not the problem here.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:44.050
First things first, where the hell are your manners?

00:12:44.430 --> 00:12:46.670
He's already in a fight with a customer!

00:12:47.340 --> 00:12:49.520
Just watch.

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:51.060
You're very calm about this...

00:12:52.110 --> 00:12:53.950
Oh, so you <i>do</i> understand.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.530
I only took my eyes off for a second.

00:12:55.530 --> 00:12:56.920
What happened?

00:12:57.850 --> 00:12:59.980
See? I told you he'd be okay.

00:13:00.250 --> 00:13:02.320
That's amazing, Haku-sama.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.820
What in the world just happened?

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:08.320
Hey, I haven't gotten my amamunii yet!

00:13:08.650 --> 00:13:10.570
Where's my damn booze!?

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:11.450
Yeah, yeah.

00:13:11.450 --> 00:13:13.280
Just be patient.

00:13:13.820 --> 00:13:17.910
Food tastes better when you're hungry, anyway.

00:13:19.020 --> 00:13:21.590
Why doesn't anybody get mad at him?

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:26.090
I guess that's just Haku for you.

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:28.630
Haku-sama is a remarkable person!

00:13:29.860 --> 00:13:32.850
Right now, it just looks like luck to me.

00:13:33.740 --> 00:13:35.720
I'll keep an eye on him.

00:13:35.720 --> 00:13:37.850
Feel free to go back.

00:13:37.850 --> 00:13:40.350
Okay. Thanks then.

00:13:41.010 --> 00:13:44.110
If you watch a bit longer, 
you might learn something.

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:46.110
About what?

00:13:53.870 --> 00:13:57.290
Don't you get tired of messing up so much?

00:13:57.760 --> 00:13:59.290
Oh, you're still here?

00:14:01.440 --> 00:14:05.440
Well, the beginning's always 
the hardest part of anything.

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:09.050
But when you're in trouble, you can just ask someone for help, right?

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:10.400
Actually, {joined}

00:14:10.400 --> 00:14:12.920
if you're just standing there watching, how about lending a hand?{joined}

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:16.810
Depending on others at the 
drop of a hat. How pathetic.

00:14:35.960 --> 00:14:40.190
How is it you can trust others so easily,

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:42.750
or just befriend anyone without a second thought?{She's kind of listing her question here, something like"How can you trust other so easily?", "How can you befriend anyone without any problem?"}{okay}

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:46.830
Well, you've made friends with Kuon, haven't you?

00:14:46.830 --> 00:14:48.630
Not at all.

00:14:49.360 --> 00:14:53.390
You can never know what others are thinking.

00:14:54.350 --> 00:14:56.890
People are selfish creatures.

00:14:56.890 --> 00:14:59.020
Of course you can't know. That's obvious.

00:14:59.390 --> 00:15:00.270
Then—

00:15:00.520 --> 00:15:03.270
But isn't that what makes things interesting?

00:15:04.700 --> 00:15:08.030
I'm not doing anything out of the ordinary.

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:11.590
The world's full of things we don't understand.

00:15:12.600 --> 00:15:14.810
It'd be a waste not to enjoy it.

00:15:17.170 --> 00:15:20.500
There's still plenty of things left in this world you don't know about.

00:15:20.880 --> 00:15:23.380
It'd be a waste not to enjoy it.

00:15:27.810 --> 00:15:29.780
<i>N-No!</i>

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.840
<i>My brother's nothing like this failure!</i>

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:35.740
Not everybody can see things the way you do!

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:36.870
Oh, c'mon.{joined}

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.970
It'd be creepy if everybody was the same, right?{joined}

00:15:40.180 --> 00:15:42.240
That's not the point—

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:43.690
Hey, Haku-san.

00:15:43.690 --> 00:15:45.210
Leave that stuff.

00:15:45.210 --> 00:15:47.690
Can you come with me and keep an eye on my kids?

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.560
Sure, on my way.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:54.740
Well, you don't need to overthink this.

00:15:55.430 --> 00:15:57.870
If you want to be friends with someone, do it.

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:58.910
Simple as that.

00:16:00.130 --> 00:16:02.000
But then you...

00:16:03.550 --> 00:16:06.130
You're weird.

00:16:06.610 --> 00:16:08.840
Man, I'm beat.

00:16:08.840 --> 00:16:11.630
I was babysitting and then the kids got all attached to me.

00:16:12.150 --> 00:16:14.450
They wouldn't let me leave.

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:16.890
They probably thought you were one of them.{wow brutal}

00:16:17.320 --> 00:16:19.250
You're so rude.

00:16:19.250 --> 00:16:23.200
Well, my pay got deducted for each thing I screwed up,

00:16:23.200 --> 00:16:25.390
but this is what I earned today.

00:16:28.650 --> 00:16:30.960
Good work, Haku-sama.

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:33.510
Yeah, good work.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:34.880
Keep at it tomorrow.

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:35.850
Yeah.

00:16:35.850 --> 00:16:36.740
Oh, right,

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:38.820
and the food they made me was good.

00:16:39.750 --> 00:16:42.300
The two of you are spoiling him.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:43.790
You're spoiling him rotten!

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:47.900
This isn't enough to pay for a single meal, 
let alone a night at an inn.

00:16:47.900 --> 00:16:49.560
You're kidding. Seriously?

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:55.050
I'm probably going to regret giving you this, but...

00:17:02.440 --> 00:17:03.640
What's this say?

00:17:05.060 --> 00:17:07.400
Haku, don't tell me you can't...

00:17:07.400 --> 00:17:09.690
You don't know how to read?

00:17:09.840 --> 00:17:11.460
I see...

00:17:11.460 --> 00:17:14.600
So all those patterns I've been seeing are letters?

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:16.200
That makes sense.

00:17:16.200 --> 00:17:17.950
I had no idea...

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:24.760
It's a real mystery to me why you don't just dump this failure, Kuon-san.

00:17:26.170 --> 00:17:28.460
Do you really have to think about it that hard?

00:17:28.710 --> 00:17:31.700
Because... problem children tend to be the cutest?

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:35.720
So what does it say?

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:40.720
"There's something I wish to speak with you about tonight, {joined}

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:44.240
so come see me."{joined}

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:45.770
Is that from Ukon?

00:17:46.430 --> 00:17:49.530
Ukon-sama's inviting Haku-sama over?

00:17:51.220 --> 00:17:54.730
At night... the two of them... under the moonlight!

00:17:54.730 --> 00:17:58.300
A-A-And then the two of them become one!

00:18:00.540 --> 00:18:02.240
Rurutie-sama!

00:18:03.970 --> 00:18:05.750
Hey, what is this place?

00:18:06.700 --> 00:18:08.050
This way.

00:18:10.320 --> 00:18:12.300
I've brought everyone.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:14.130
Oh, come in.

00:18:14.130 --> 00:18:15.900
Excuse us.

00:18:15.900 --> 00:18:17.700
Thank you for coming.

00:18:17.700 --> 00:18:18.820
Oshutaru!

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:23.390
My thanks for your assistance in dealing with those bandits.

00:18:23.860 --> 00:18:27.680
Wait, wasn't it Ukon who asked us to come here?

00:18:27.680 --> 00:18:29.880
I shall get right to the point.

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:33.210
I wish to become your patron.

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:38.030
For reasons I cannot speak of yet, I require a man I can trust.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:41.150
I spoke with my friend,

00:18:41.150 --> 00:18:43.030
and he recommended you.

00:18:43.280 --> 00:18:44.370
Your friend?

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:47.980
A talented herbalist who is no stranger to battle.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.690
A man who, combat abilities notwithstanding, {check this}

00:18:50.690 --> 00:18:54.040
possesses the sharpest of minds and a mysterious charisma.

00:18:54.530 --> 00:18:59.050
He hadn't known you long, 
but he spoke very highly of you.

00:18:59.530 --> 00:19:00.580
<i>I see.</i>

00:19:00.580 --> 00:19:02.950
<i>This "friend" is Ukon, huh?</i>

00:19:02.950 --> 00:19:04.690
So you sent that letter?

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:07.180
Maroro gave you his highest recommendation.

00:19:07.620 --> 00:19:08.710
I'm sure you're the one.

00:19:08.710 --> 00:19:09.930
<i>It was him!?</i>

00:19:10.570 --> 00:19:14.500
Naturally, I was planning to tell you this from the start.

00:19:15.180 --> 00:19:17.880
What, still haven't figured it out?

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.290
And here I thought we were supposed to be friends.

00:19:20.290 --> 00:19:21.070
What?

00:19:21.500 --> 00:19:23.930
The young miss realized, though.

00:19:23.930 --> 00:19:25.070
That's right.

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:28.140
{}It was when I saw you in town.

00:19:28.560 --> 00:19:29.970
Crying shame.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.000
I wanted to surprise you a bit more.

00:19:37.570 --> 00:19:38.530
Ukon!

00:19:38.530 --> 00:19:39.620
Yep.

00:19:39.620 --> 00:19:41.660
Ukon is a fake identity.

00:19:41.660 --> 00:19:45.640
My true identity is 
General of the Right, Oshutaru-sama.

00:19:46.850 --> 00:19:48.140
You?

00:19:48.140 --> 00:19:50.640
Are you sure about this, Big Brother?

00:19:50.940 --> 00:19:53.580
Kuon-san maybe, but this man is...

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:56.220
You thought he was good enough, didn't you?

00:19:56.220 --> 00:19:58.650
See? Interesting guy, ain't he?

00:19:59.180 --> 00:20:00.780
W-Well...

00:20:08.430 --> 00:20:10.500
Baths really are the best.

00:20:10.500 --> 00:20:11.940
I agree.

00:20:11.940 --> 00:20:13.290
Right?

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:17.520
You've really done a lot for Haku.

00:20:17.520 --> 00:20:19.540
Don't worry about it.

00:20:22.620 --> 00:20:27.320
This murky water is so good for your skin.

00:20:28.490 --> 00:20:31.150
Sulfur is good for your circulation.

00:20:31.150 --> 00:20:33.730
Wow, where'd you learn that?

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:37.430
It just happened to be a topic of study once.

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:40.730
Maybe I'll treat you to 
something nice after our bath.

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.070
Some nice cold milk, for instance?

00:20:44.070 --> 00:20:46.240
I'd gulp it right down!

00:20:47.450 --> 00:20:49.070
You know how it works, I see!

00:20:49.070 --> 00:20:50.960
I could say the same to you.

00:20:55.310 --> 00:20:58.940
<i>I hate to admit that he's the one who taught me this,</i>

00:20:58.940 --> 00:21:00.920
<i>but I don't have to overthink it.</i>

00:21:00.920 --> 00:21:03.760
<i>I should just do what feels right.</i>

00:21:06.050 --> 00:21:08.940
I hope we can get along,{split}

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:10.030
{my sister}Big Sister.{split}

00:21:11.180 --> 00:21:12.640
Of course!

00:22:58.810 --> 00:23:01.830
Welcome back, you two.

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:03.120
Come inside.

00:23:07.230 --> 00:23:11.270
You're certain that you've found him?

00:23:12.540 --> 00:23:13.930
I see...

00:23:13.930 --> 00:23:17.260
My lord, at last... at long last...

00:23:17.520 --> 00:23:19.210
It's been so long.

00:23:19.210 --> 00:23:22.020
How long have I waited for this day?

00:23:22.470 --> 00:23:26.020
It must be by the grace of Heaven{split}

00:23:26.020 --> 00:23:28.800
that he has appeared before my life ends.{split}
